formNestT -- a form inside a field, G2 stroke 1b (Tony, 2026-11-13). Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh.
A field written form:=other is the frame for that form: layout gives the field its frame, lays the form out in it
(incant/utilities placeForm, through setFrame) and hangs the laid-out copy under the field; the draw walk draws it there.

NF-1  npOuter: npHost sits between a 40-point head and a 40-point foot, so its frame is 400x320 at 0,40, and the
      descriptions form laid out inside it has exactly that frame. On the page (10,50) is the held form's lightGreen
      heading field and (10,380) is npFoot's white.
NF-2  a second run reads as the first: the same frame for the held form.
NF-3  TWO FIELDS, ONE FORM: npLeft and npRight both hold descriptions; each gets its own copy, 200 wide, at x 0 and x 200,
      and both draw (lightGreen at (10,10) and (210,10)). One shared copy could sit in only one of the two places.
NF-4  A FORM THAT HOLDS ITSELF is refused by name at layout and its field is left empty: npIn is rewritten to hold npSelf
      (a := in a define cannot name its own form: the name is not defined yet, and the define refuses it). The page is
      still drawn (npSelf's wall at (10,10)), and the list of forms being laid out is empty afterwards.
NF-5  firstLight holds descriptions in its lower half: heading's wall at (300,15), the held form's lightGreen heading
      field at (10,210), ok's green at (390,190).
H7: with placeForm's call removed from frameMembers, NF-1, NF-3 and NF-5 go red.
